  "description": "JATBUF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C81 H88 Dy6 N18 O20 6+,C1 H4 O1,6(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.518-3.832 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.49-110.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-O)(μ3-OH)4(L2)3(L3)3(L4)3(H2O)3]Cl6·CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
